,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,-------------::::;ii++ ++++++hhHH$@ @MHhh++ii;;;;;ihi;:---,,,,,,,,,,,,.........&#10; .....,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,--------------:::;;;;;;iiii++h *h+ii;;;;:::::::----,,,,,,,,,,,...........&#10; .....,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,---------------::::;;;;;ii+hM@ $hii;;:::::::------,,,,,,,,,,,............&#10; .......,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,---------------::::::;;;+ *@ +i;::::::-------,,,,,,,,,,,..............&#10; ........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,---------------::::::;i+HhH *h++;;::::---------,,,,,,,,,,................&#10; .........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,--------------::::::;;ii+hH* $H+ii;:::---------,,,,,,,,,,..................&#10; .........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,-------------:::::;;i+hM MM #+;;:---------,,,,,,,,,,....................&#10; ...........,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,------------::::;;+# hiiii :---------,,,,,,,,,.......................&#10; .............,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,----------:::;ih$+;;::::-------,,,,,,,,,..........................&#10; ...............,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,---------:i;;::::-------,,,,,,,,,.............................&#10; .................,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,----------,,,,,,,,,,,,.................................&#10; .....................,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,......................................&#10; ..........................,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.............................................&#10; ...................................,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,.......................................................&#10; .........................................................................................................&#10; .......................................................................................................&#10; .....................................................................................................&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;I amended the code to update the OLED I was using in the temperature sensor tests &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/mand_oled.py"&gt;mand_oled&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Pico W Temperature</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico3/</link><pubDate>Tue, 17 Jan 2023 12:29:22 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico3/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Have been tinkering with temperature measurement using the Raspberry Pi Pico.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;First with the internal temperature sensor and then using a TMP36 temperature sensor externally.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I wrote two classes to access these and return the reading.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/library/internal_temp.py"&gt;Internal Temperature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/library/tmp36.py"&gt;External Temperature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is an example using the two sensors together &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/temps.py"&gt;temps.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You will need to upload the two classes to the Pico first in a &lt;code&gt;library&lt;/code&gt; sub-directory.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is how you would wire it up on a breadboard &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/circuits/tmp36.fzz"&gt;tmp36.fzz&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rasberry Pi Pico W OLED</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico2/</link><pubDate>Tue, 10 Jan 2023 13:38:21 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico2/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Some components arrived from AliExpress recently so been able to play with an I2C OLED display with my Pico W.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Hello World Test&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="wp-caption alignnone"&gt;&#10; &lt;a data-flickr-embed="true" data-header="true" data-footer="false"&#10; data-context="false"&#10; href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/52611812353"&#10; title="Hello World"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52611812353_596b54ceff_c.jpg" width="800" alt="Hello World" /&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;script async src="//embedr.flickr.com/assets/client-code.js" charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text"&gt;Hello World Test&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Code of this is here &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/i2c_scan.py"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/i2c_scan.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;And also used here to display the IP address after connected to the wifi &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/wifi_oled.py"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/wifi_oled.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Next thing I&amp;rsquo;ve been playing with is internal and external temperature sensors, I will post about that soon.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Pico W</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Jan 2023 13:31:23 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Just before Christmas I got a Raspberry Pi Pico W to have a play with.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Looking forward to using MicroPython to do some LED flashing and other things.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Started a repo on Github for it &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w"&gt;Pico W Repo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>#RaspberryPi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberrypi/</link><pubDate>Wed, 02 Mar 2016 20:54:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberrypi/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://farm2.staticflickr.com/1442/25082856179_7b47f97c92_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;via Instagram &lt;a href="http://ift.tt/1QskMQB" rel="nofollow"&gt;ift.tt/1QskMQB&lt;/a&gt; March 02, 2016 at 08:52PM http://flic.kr/p/Educgz, March 02, 2016 at 08:52PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi 3 #RaspberryPi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-3-raspberrypi/</link><pubDate>Wed, 02 Mar 2016 20:54:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/raspberry-pi-3-raspberrypi/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://farm2.staticflickr.com/1476/24819919394_e13b1a2cd4_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;via Instagram &lt;a href="http://ift.tt/1WVoINv" rel="nofollow"&gt;ift.tt/1WVoINv&lt;/a&gt; March 02, 2016 at 08:52PM http://flic.kr/p/DPfzjJ, March 02, 2016 at 08:53PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Let the fun begin #RaspberryPi</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/let-fun-begin-raspberrypi/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Mar 2016 20:40:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/let-fun-begin-raspberrypi/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://farm2.staticflickr.com/1514/25297314242_030de533db_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;via Instagram &lt;a href="http://ift.tt/1XYroLq" rel="nofollow"&gt;ift.tt/1XYroLq&lt;/a&gt; March 01, 2016 at 07:14PM http://flic.kr/p/Exrmbo, March 01, 2016 at 07:14PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Juicessh on Nexus 5</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/juicessh-on-nexus-5/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Feb 2014 21:47:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/juicessh-on-nexus-5/</guid><description>&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm4.staticflickr.com/3754/12507561885_fa837b3711_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Controlling mpd and icecast2 on my Raspberry Pi http://flic.kr/p/k4fwoH, February 13, 2014 at 09:26PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>R